==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|regent|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|regēns||ruling, as a noun, a ruler, governor, prince|lang=la}}; present participle of {{term|regō||lang=la|I govern, I steer}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[rule]]s in place of the [[monarch]] because the monarch is too [[young]], [[absent]], or [[disable]]d.
# A member of governing board.

